---
import ChatAvatar from '@/components/chat-avatar.astro';
import Layout from '@/components/layout.astro';

import clara from '@/assets/clara.png';
import orchestrator from '@/assets/orchestrator.png';
import theo from '@/assets/theo.png';

const description =
  "Collegium runs LLM agents as members of your team's chat, handling email, research, and follow-through, with a human approving anything consequential.";

const postures = [
  {
    body: "Agents live in your team's channels. The work, the tool calls, the questions, and the results all land in the conversation. If work is happening, there is a post you can scroll to.",
    title: 'Everything Happens in Your Chat'
  },
  {
    body: 'Anything that leaves a mark stops and asks first: the exact email before it is sent, the exact file before it is written. You see the full payload, then approve it, deny it, or deny it with a reason the agent can act on.',
    title: 'Consequential Actions Wait for You'
  },
  {
    body: 'An agent holds exactly the tools its role requires and nothing more. There is no shell access by default, and no way for an agent to grow its own reach. What an agent can touch is a fact you can read in its configuration.',
    title: 'Capabilities Are Granted, Never Ambient'
  },
  {
    body: 'Agents act when a person addresses them, or when deterministic code you configured announces work. Never on their own initiative. And when anything goes wrong, they stop and say so: no silent retries, no improvised workarounds, no quietly degraded answers.',
    title: 'Deterministic Starts, Clean Stops'
  }
];

const refusals = [
  {
    body: 'Nothing happens unless a person addresses an agent, or a trigger you configured announces work in the channel. The cost: idle agents do nothing. That is the point. An agent with initiative and idle cycles finds work nobody asked for.',
    title: "Agents Don't Schedule Themselves"
  },
  {
    body: 'No agent can edit its own instructions, tools, or schedule. The cost: improving an agent is your change to make, not something the system learns on its own. In return, the agent you reviewed yesterday is the agent running today.',
    title: "Agents Don't Modify Themselves"
  },
  {
    body: 'Every actor has a durable name, and its work is in a channel. The cost: throughput. Big jobs proceed one visible conversation at a time, not as a swarm. In return, nothing is ever done by a worker that no longer exists to answer for it.',
    title: "Agents Don't Spawn Workers"
  },
  {
    body: 'A denied action, a malformed response, an ambiguous outcome: each one ends the turn with a visible notice. In a coding agent, retrying a flaky call is helpful. When the flaky call was an email to your client, a retry is a duplicate email. We would rather interrupt you than be quietly wrong for six hours.',
    title: 'Agents Stop Instead of Degrading'
  }
];

const claraTrace = [
  { detail: 'opened "Sponsoring Northshore Summit 2027" from elena@northshoresummit.co', tool: 'mail' },
  { detail: 'northshore summit 2026: silver tier, booth skipped', tool: 'read_memory' }
];

const theoTrace = [{ detail: 'northshoresummit.co → Sponsors → 2027 tiers', tool: 'browser' }];
---

<Layout description={description} title="Collegium">
  <main class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-4xl flex-1 flex-col gap-24 px-6 py-20 sm:py-28">
    <section class="flex flex-col items-start gap-6">
      <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground font-mono text-sm tracking-wide">Collegium</span>
      <h1 class="max-w-3xl text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">
        Agents you supervise like people, not services.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-fd-muted-foreground max-w-2xl text-lg sm:text-xl">
        Collegium agents are members of your team's chat, each with its own name, tools, and memory. They handle the
        work that isn't writing software, like email, research, and follow-through.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          class="bg-fd-primary text-fd-primary-foreground hover:bg-fd-primary/90 rounded-lg px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium transition-colors"
          href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart"
        >
          Quickstart
        </a>
        <a
          class="border-fd-border hover:bg-fd-accent rounded-lg border px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium transition-colors"
          href="https://github.com/joshunrau/collegium"
          rel="noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
        >
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        postures.map((posture) => (
          <div class="border-fd-border bg-fd-card flex flex-col gap-2 rounded-xl border p-5">
            <span class="font-medium">{posture.title}</span>
            <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-sm">{posture.body}</span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Why It's Built This Way</h2>
      <p class="text-fd-muted-foreground max-w-3xl">
        Most agent frameworks share one shape: give a model a shell and let it iterate unattended until the task looks
        done. That shape was built for writing software, where a failed attempt costs nothing and every change is
        reviewable as a diff before it ships.
      </p>
      <p class="text-fd-muted-foreground max-w-3xl">
        Business work is different. Actions are visible to clients and colleagues the moment they happen, many cannot be
        taken back, and nobody reviews them line by line afterward. So Collegium refuses four things autonomous
        frameworks celebrate, and each refusal is the point.
      </p>
      <ul class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        {
          refusals.map((refusal) => (
            <li class="flex flex-col gap-2">
              <span class="font-medium">{refusal.title}</span>
              <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground max-w-3xl text-sm">{refusal.body}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="max-w-3xl">
        And instead of autonomy, you get a system that runs your business logic as code. A procedure that matters is not
        a prompt instruction the model might skip on a bad day. It is a plugin: deterministic TypeScript you write once,
        review once, and grant to the agents that need it. It will not change under you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How It Works</h2>
      <p class="text-fd-muted-foreground max-w-2xl">
        One job, end to end. An email arrives, Clara owns the reply, Theo digs up the facts, and a person approves the
        send. Everything below is a channel you could scroll.
      </p>

      <div class="border-fd-border bg-fd-card flex flex-col gap-7 rounded-xl border p-5 sm:p-6">
        <article class="flex gap-3">
          <ChatAvatar image={orchestrator} />
          <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-2">
            <p class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <span class="text-sm font-medium">Orchestrator</span>
              <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs">10:02 AM</span>
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm">
              New mail for <span class="bg-fd-accent text-fd-accent-foreground rounded px-1 py-0.5 font-medium">
                @clara
              </span>
            </p>
            <div class="border-fd-border bg-fd-background rounded-lg border text-sm">
              <dl class="border-fd-border grid gap-1 border-b px-4 py-3 sm:grid-cols-[4rem_1fr]">
                <dt class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs">From</dt>
                <dd class="text-sm">elena@northshoresummit.co</dd>
                <dt class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs">Subject</dt>
                <dd class="text-sm">Sponsoring Northshore Summit 2027</dd>
              </dl>
              <p class="text-fd-muted-foreground px-4 py-3">
                Hi! Planning for next June has started, and we'd love to have you back as a sponsor. This year's tiers
                are up on our site. Any interest in returning?
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="flex gap-3">
          <ChatAvatar image={clara} />
          <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-2">
            <p class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <span class="text-sm font-medium">Clara</span>
              <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs">10:02 AM</span>
            </p>
            <ul class="border-fd-border flex flex-col gap-1.5 border-l pl-3">
              {
                claraTrace.map((line) => (
                  <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 text-xs">
                    <code class="font-mono">{line.tool}</code>
                    <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground">{line.detail}</span>
                  </li>
                ))
              }
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="flex gap-3">
          <ChatAvatar image={clara} />
          <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-2">
            <p class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <span class="text-sm font-medium">Clara</span>
              <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs">10:03 AM</span>
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm">
              <span class="bg-fd-accent text-fd-accent-foreground rounded px-1 py-0.5 font-medium">@theo</span> can you pull
              the 2027 sponsor tiers from northshoresummit.co? I need silver's price and what it includes.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="flex gap-3">
          <ChatAvatar image={theo} />
          <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-2">
            <p class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <span class="text-sm font-medium">Theo</span>
              <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs">10:03 AM</span>
            </p>
            <ul class="border-fd-border flex flex-col gap-1.5 border-l pl-3">
              {
                theoTrace.map((line) => (
                  <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 text-xs">
                    <code class="font-mono">{line.tool}</code>
                    <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground">{line.detail}</span>
                  </li>
                ))
              }
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="flex gap-3">
          <ChatAvatar image={theo} />
          <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-2">
            <p class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <span class="text-sm font-medium">Theo</span>
              <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs">10:05 AM</span>
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm">
              <span class="bg-fd-accent text-fd-accent-foreground rounded px-1 py-0.5 font-medium">@clara</span> Silver is
              $4,000 for 2027: logo placement, two passes, and a careers-page listing. Gold is $8,500 and adds a booth. Silver
              is up $500 from last year.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="flex gap-3">
          <ChatAvatar image={clara} />
          <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-2">
            <p class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <span class="text-sm font-medium">Clara</span>
              <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs">10:06 AM</span>
            </p>
            <div class="border-fd-border bg-fd-background rounded-lg border">
              <p class="border-fd-border text-fd-muted-foreground border-b px-4 py-2.5 font-mono text-xs tracking-wide">
                approval required · send mail
              </p>
              <dl class="border-fd-border grid gap-1 border-b px-4 py-3 sm:grid-cols-[4rem_1fr]">
                <dt class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs">To</dt>
                <dd class="text-sm">elena@northshoresummit.co</dd>
                <dt class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs">Subject</dt>
                <dd class="text-sm">Re: Sponsoring Northshore Summit 2027</dd>
              </dl>
              <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 px-4 py-3 text-sm">
                <p>Hi Elena,</p>
                <p>
                  Good to hear from you. We had a great experience last year and would like to return at silver. I see
                  it is $4,000 for 2027; could you send the agreement over? One request: we'd like the careers-page
                  listing live ahead of the conference this time.
                </p>
                <p>Thanks,</p>
                <p>Clara</p>
              </div>
              <div class="border-fd-border flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t px-4 py-3">
                <span class="bg-fd-primary text-fd-primary-foreground rounded-md px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium">
                  Approve
                </span>
                <span class="border-fd-border rounded-md border px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium">Deny</span>
                <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs sm:ml-auto">Approved by maya · 10:31 AM</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="flex gap-3">
          <ChatAvatar image={clara} />
          <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-2">
            <p class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <span class="text-sm font-medium">Clara</span>
              <span class="text-fd-muted-foreground text-xs">10:31 AM</span>
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm">Sent. I noted the $500 increase for next year's budgeting.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="text-fd-muted-foreground max-w-3xl">
        The announcement is deterministic code, not an agent deciding your mail matters. The approval shows the entire
        payload: every recipient, the full body, nothing summarized. And the send happens exactly once or not at all: an
        ambiguous outcome stops the turn rather than retrying your client's inbox.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col items-start gap-6">
      <p class="max-w-2xl text-lg">See it running in ten minutes.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          class="bg-fd-primary text-fd-primary-foreground hover:bg-fd-primary/90 rounded-lg px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium transition-colors"
          href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart"
        >
          Quickstart
        </a>
        <a
          class="border-fd-border hover:bg-fd-accent rounded-lg border px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium transition-colors"
          href="https://github.com/joshunrau/collegium"
          rel="noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
        >
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
